1
00:00:00,847 --> 00:00:03,767
(Howard:)-I totally had a shot.
-With a woman you were chasing in a park.

2
00:00:03,934 --> 00:00:05,604
(Raj:)That's not a shot, that's a felony.

3
00:00:07,896 --> 00:00:11,436
(Raj:)What's worse, it cost me
my prized Patang fighting kite.

4
00:00:12,025 --> 00:00:15,485
(Raj:)I don't suppose there's any chance
you could give me my kite back?

5
00:00:15,904 --> 00:00:18,904
(Sheldon:)I'm sorry, Raj,
but the rules of aerial warfare dictate...

6
00:00:19,074 --> 00:00:21,074
...that the fallen kite go to the victor.

7
00:00:21,243 --> 00:00:23,743
(Sheldon:)And without rules,
the competition has no meaning.

8
00:00:23,912 --> 00:00:26,952
(Sheldon:)And without meaning, the following
would be an empty gesture:

9
00:00:27,416 --> 00:00:31,416
[SINGSONGY]
I have your kite, I have your kite

10
00:00:38,427 --> 00:00:39,887
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

11
00:00:40,053 --> 00:00:41,133
(Penny:)-Hey.
-Hi.

12
00:00:41,305 --> 00:00:42,635
(Leonard:)How was your football party?

13
00:00:42,806 --> 00:00:45,976
(Penny:)-It was pretty good, we won.
-Oh, wow, that's excellent.

14
00:00:46,143 --> 00:00:47,853
Weird figure of speech, isn't it?

15
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:50,900
"We won,"
when you weren't actually playing.

16
00:00:52,190 --> 00:00:55,610
When we watch Star Wars, we don't say,
"We defeated the Empire." Ha, ha.

17
00:00:57,070 --> 00:00:59,070
(Penny:)I'm glad to hear it.

18
00:00:59,990 --> 00:01:01,370
(Leonard:)Oh, hey, on a related subject...

